+			when(BedrockKnowledgeBaseVectorStoreTest.this.mockClient.retrieve(any(RetrieveRequest.class)))
+				.thenReturn(RetrieveResponse.builder().retrievalResults(List.of()).build());
+
+			// When
+			storeWithSemantic.similaritySearch(SearchRequest.builder().query("test").build());
+
+			// Then
+			ArgumentCaptor<RetrieveRequest> captor = ArgumentCaptor.forClass(RetrieveRequest.class);
+			verify(BedrockKnowledgeBaseVectorStoreTest.this.mockClient).retrieve(captor.capture());
+
+			assertThat(captor.getValue().retrievalConfiguration().vectorSearchConfiguration().overrideSearchType())
+				.isEqualTo(SearchType.SEMANTIC);
+		}
+
+	}
+
+}

Below is the change description:
To provide native integration with Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases, enabling users to perform Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) operations leveraging Bedrock's fully managed service. This solution offloads document ingestion, chunking, and embedding management to AWS, and provides a standardized VectorStore abstraction that users can integrate into their existing Spring AI applications.
Introduced a new implementation of the VectorStore interface for Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases. This includes a new library (spring-ai-bedrock-knowledgebase-store), a corresponding Spring Boot auto-configuration module (spring-ai-autoconfigure-vector-store-bedrock-knowledgebase), and a starter dependency (spring-ai-starter-vector-store-bedrock-knowledgebase). The implementation allows performing similarity searches against an existing AWS Bedrock Knowledge Base and includes support for metadata filtering, reranking, and hybrid search configurations.

